          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Ernest Rutherford</strong><br>\nErnest Rutherford was born on August 30, 1871, in Nelson, New Zealand, as one of 12 children in a farmer's family. He showed early signs of interest in science and won a scholarship to Nelson College, where he excelled in mathematics and science. Later, he earned another scholarship to attend the University of New Zealand, where he continued to demonstrate his potential in scientific research by graduating with a degree in physical sciences.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Move to England and Nobel Prize</strong><br>\nIn 1895, Rutherford was awarded a scholarship to Cambridge University in England to work at the Cavendish Laboratory under J.J. Thomson. His work on detecting radio waves earned him a Nobel Prize in Chemistry in 1908 for his investigations into the disintegration of the elements and the chemistry of radioactive substances.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Discoveries in Radioactivity</strong><br>\nWhile at McGill University in Montreal, Rutherford discovered that thorium released a gas that was itself radioactive, which he named \"thoron.\" This led to the understanding that radioactive substances can transmute into other elements, laying the groundwork for the field of nuclear chemistry.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
